re: Windows trademark/patent.

Could Ford or GM name a vehicle "CARS" or "AUTOMOBILES" ? or "WHEELS" ?

Remember that APPLE was well ahead to the market with the introduction
of a windows based machine called LISA. (prior to the MACintosh).

The problem with WINDOWS as a trade mark is that it also describes a
concept which is not patentable or which is already owned by someone
else (XEROX or APPLE). Apple did sue Microsoft over the similarities of
the WINDOWS gui to that of the MAC (FILE MENU, position of buttons
controlling the window position/size etc etc).

Personally, I do not think that IBM should have ever been granted the
word "PC". A generic term now becoming a corporate trade mark. Windows
was a generic term that became a MS trademark.



