my roommate has a compaq with a "special" compaq  keyboard that has the
spacebar split in two and the left half of it is actually backspace.

it took me a while to figure out what was going on, since when do you
actually look down at what you are typing to see if the key you expect
to be there is actually there?

My $.02 about keyboards, top three in order are:

MIT superkeyboard that I read about in the Jargon File, no less than 
7 different activating keys, (ctrl, alt, shift, meta, top, left, right)
and a suite of applications to utilize them.  kind of out of fashion
now except for the keystroke thing (emacs anyone?)

chorded keyboard.  tough to learn, can't type too fast, but kiss carpal
tunnel and repetitive stress goodbye.  plus which it has a cool factor
of about 23.

dvorak keyboard.  Now there is a good idea.  why aren't they more
standard?  I mean really, it would make a lot of things a lot easier.
hey, I have convinced myself.  I am going to go out and learn to type
dvorak, save my wrists for future use.

-eric

