Ideally, it should be possible for the user to choose from a set of
configurations
or reset them to their liking, as EMACS does. Ideally, it should also be
possible
for non-programmer to learn how make these changes quickly and easily, 
unlike EMACS. The 'Kitchen Sink' is arguably the best general text
editor even 
after 20 years, but its huge size and arcane control structure puts it
out of reach of
most users, even the X and MS-Windoze versions. Of course, MS-Word even
bigger,
and  is at least as overengineered... its remarkable that they expect
casual users
to navigate that thicket of commands, even programmers I know can get
lost in the 
