Zalman Stern <zalman@netcom.com> wrote:
>Joe Buck (jbuck@synopsys.com) wrote:
>[BetaMax vs. VHS.]
>
>Wasn't VHS originally developed by RCA?
>
>-Z-

   No, VHS was developed by JVC, a division of
Matsushita after they rejected Sony's offering
of their Beta format  after several meetings
between the two companies.  Read about it in
"Made In Japan", a book by Sony founder Akio
Morita.  RCA was an early adopter of VHS and
invented the non-standard 4hr LP speed which
is not part of the official VHS standard.

  Sounds similar to the DEC/Intel Alpha
meetings.  However, Japanese video companies
have cross licensing agreements for the use
of video patents.  This worked out to Sony's
disadvantage since they came up with many/most
of the innovations (HiFi, enhanced video
SuperBeta, real-time counters, crystal clear
effects, the camcorder) and the market was willing 
to wait the year and a half for these things to 
show up on VHS.

--
Vance Haemmerle
