Apologies in advance if one or more of the rather eclectic
set of newsgroups is off-target, but I wasn't able to find
one that seemed exactly correct ...

We have an application that requires a moderate number of
P200, P200 Pro, Alpha, or Power PC processors.  (Which CPU
we choose will depend primarily on which provides the best
performance for the amount of money we have available for
this project.)

All we need is CPU, memory, and ethernet.  No need for a
disk, video card, monitor, keyboard, mouse, etc.

Our first approach was to look at the same source we use
for our Pentium-based PCs, and buying some stripped-down
variant of what we've bought before, eliminating all the
components we don't need.

However, it occurs to me that perhaps we might do better
by buying a bunch of some type of single-board computer,
and an enclosure/rack/whatever which could house them all
and supply power.

The problem is that all the suppliers I've checked seem
to sell SBCs which have a lot of features that we don't
have any use for (on-board IDE/EIDE controller, floppy
controller, ISA bus, parallel port, etc.), and lack the
one item we *do* need, a 10BaseT ethernet port.

I realize that our needs are somewhat nonstandard (maybe
"off-beat" would be a better term), but perhaps someone
may know of a company that caters to this sort of niche
market.

Many thanks in advance.

