The key to Galaxies is performance a factor of 10 (conservatively!) better
than ANY other OS, on the same iron, gained by using VMS instead of
some other OS. The NDA showed this. It is not smoke & mirrors, or
a projection. Galaxies is real technology, and completely new.

That bottom line is true for nearly all loads, though there is a
"subset of zero measure" of loads that are so heavily compute bound
and need so little communication that competing NUMA or MPP systems
can do as well. Not better...at most as well.

The speculation about "improved memory channel" is wrong; the communication
is much faster than that.

To understand the whole problem it is necessary to understand data 
reliability issues and what the inherent limitations of SMP are,
among other things. But remember the bottom line: put any other
OS on the iron and run at 10% the speed of VMS. And maybe have a
system that stays up far less of the time...




