Let's not forget those folks with medical problems...

Many years back, I wrote a graphical post-processor
for a chemical thermo code.  It was the first time I
had ever done mouse programming, so I went a little
overboard (gee, maybe those Mac users had something!).

Then my wife pointed out that one of the principal
users of the code had multiple sclerosis, and 
another was arthritic; for these people, key combinations
were greatly preferred to mouse movements.  Several
other users ran the code from laptops with trackballs, and
greatly preferred key combos to the trackball.

I've noticed that many graphics/CAD programs
no longer allow screen movements via the cursor keys.
I really, really miss the precision I can get, placing the
cursor in the exact upper left hand corner of a bit map...
vs. the spastic fight with the mouse to get that top 
left pixel, invariably turning the pointer into a "resize"
icon just when I think I'm done...



