and decided that TotalImpact's SMP PowerPC cards were my
best bet.  They don't have the extraneous bus controllers,
but unfortunately they also don't have an ethernet port.
What I'd suggest would be to write a device driver which
allows them to use an ethernet card which is plugged into
the same computer that they are.  (The platform I'd like 
to develop would be a PCI-based IBM PC with three or four 
of TotalImpact's SMP cards plugged into it; the ethernet 
card could then be plugged into an ISA slot, and the linux 
kernel running on the PC would route packets appropriately 
either between different cards on the same PCI bus, or 
between different systems on the ethernet network.)

