Costomiris) wrote:

>I recently acquired a vt420 that I planned to use while doing OS installs on
>Sparcs.  Just a bit of a problem with it, however.  I expected to find a 
>DB25, or even a DB9 on the back, which I'd use to jack in to the serial port.
>
>I only have a pair of RJ-11-ish looking jacks (the kb is an RJ-11).

Those are called MMJ (Modified Modular Jack?)

>
>On the right is a jack labled "1", and on the left is a jack labled "2", 
>which also has a small picture of a printer.  There's a plastic panel 
>covering a hole that says "Comm 1" (or somesuch, it's not in front of me
>at the moment), however, when I pulled the plate out, there's no port.

The VT420 supports two comm sessions at the same time, or 1
session and a printer (unless you have the software to do
two sessions over one serial poprt and use the other port
for printer. There was a version that had an RS232 25 pin
port instead of that cover connected to port 1, but I don't
know if adding the connector to the board will work or not.
You could try to trace out the lines. The 1 is port 1. The 2
is port 2 or the printer port (serial).

>
>I assume the kb would get plugged in to jack #1, and then I'd need some
>sort of adapter to go to jack #2, and take it to DB25, so I can slap
>on the cable/null modem adapter.  Am I correct in thinking this?  Or did I
>just inherit a doorstop?

The keyboard plugs into an RJ11 port on the right (?) side
of the tube, toward the front. Those two ports are for data
communications only. The pinout for the adapter is available
in the VMS FAQ. (I don't have a location for this right now,
sorry.)

