Speaking of ergonomics, those bent microsoft keyboards are about
the worst affront to ergonomics I've ever seen.  First off,
they are needlessly too thick, which means that even the
thinest desk top doesn't elevates the keyboard too high
above the proper position (and still allows my legs
underneath).

Second, the angle between the two halves is designed for
someone who's either much fatter or has much shorter
arms than me.  In order to get my fingers on the keys
I have to hold my elbows way out from my sides.  I
once saw one that was actually articulated in the
middle (I think it was a Mac) which might actually
work, but I'll stick with a more ergonomically
chosen straight keyboard for now.



