The VT420 is a dual session terminal. Com1 and Com2 can both be used for
ASCII sessions. I used each on a dual VAXcluster as consoles.

If one wishes, one can use Com2 for a printer and then the dual session
capability is available through Com1 and special software on OpenVMS or on
a DECserver.

We use a nice cable in this connector and you can purchase an adapter that
the jack on the end of the cable will plug into and voila, you have a DB25
pin connector.

The keyboard goes into the small RJ11 jack, golly, been so long, but I do
believe it's around the side of the terminal, in any event, it does have a
little keyboard ICON beside it.

