Subject: Re: HELP!  Digital DEC pc 425 windows 3.1 diagnosis --(System Configuration Error - RUN SETUP)
Date: 1997/05/28
Message-ID: <rtt-2805972237240001@piccolo-46.synapse.net>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 244623673
References: <H.Micklem-ya023080002305970010210001@newsread.ed.ac.uk>
Organization: neuron, technology consultants
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Possibly the CMOS battery is now dead given the machines age. On these
systems when they started up, they would give this message until memory
had been sized and set in the CMOS. If the battery were dead, it would
never retain the sizing of memory.
In addition, your copy of MS-DOS and Windows on the machine is hosed and
you would be best advised to do a complete virgin install, partition the
disk, format it and start the MS-DOS install from scratch.

CMOS batteries can be obtained as replacements practically anywhere there
is an electronics store.

rtt



