> You've read the quotes, Digital are not interested in licencing the
> technology of the Alpha, they "just want Intel to stop producing
> Pentium-based procesors". Whether they will get what they want, well who
> knows, but if they do...

The more I think about it, the more I don't think the courts can halt
Pentium shipments.  This would be too much of a hardship on the
computer-buying public.  Sure there is AMD and Cyrix, and it appears
that K6 and M2 are fast enough for all applications to which x86
processors are applied; however, AMD and Cyrix combined don't have a
fraction of the capacity to satisfy demand, and if demand for Intel
alternatives soars the prices will also soar.

The court could possibly instruct Intel to remove the offending
technologies as quickly as possible, while paying tolerable fines and
penalties to Digital; but they can't ask Intel to simply stop shipping
Pentiums.  The damage done would be to you and me.

