Mike, even without being totally au fait with this setup, it looks to me
like a DMA request is failing, as if the DMA controller for the drive is
programming a memory burst to an address block that doesn't exist.
Perhaps it is the *controller* settings you should look at, rather than
the drive. Have you got memory maps for the two machines, ie the one you
pulled it from, and the one you put it into? Maybe the memory map on the
original was substantially different to your current one.

