In article <5m7umd$h85@nyx.cs.du.edu>,
Gary Heston <gheston@nyx.cs.du.edu> wrote:
>>My biggest problem is my complete unfamiliarity with the machine.  I am
>>under the impression that this is the only VAX with this backplane, and
>>know of no repository of net wisdom on the beast.  I've got a KA820-AA CPU,
>>MS820-CA RAM, the DEBNT card and a TK-50, an AIO card (huh?) and a KA-800
>>(dunno what that is either).  I've got the E&S hardware too but don't know
>>what VMS is required to support it, nor what the required monitor should be.
>
>If you've got a DEBNT, then you've got a BI cage. Is there something else
>feeding that? (I have an XMI bus, which interfaces to the two small BI
>cages and the BA-11 chassis with individual adapter cards.)

  There wouldn't be anything else driving that BI bus.  The KA820 CPU
is a BI-based CPU; the same as is used in the VAX 8200.  This machine
is basically a VAX 8200 in a different chassis with a framebuffer.

  You might want to try replacing the KA820 with a KA825 (a little
faster, via better microcode I believe)...it's a drop-in replacement
and can be found very cheaply.  You can also drop one or more
additional processor boards in the backplane.  VMS will deal with it,
and I believe Ultrix will as well.  Basically:

  1x KA820 is a VAX 8200
  2x KA820 is a VAX 8300
  1x KA825 is a VAX 8250
  2x KA825 is a VAX 8350


