Stephen Hoff Hoffman wrote:
> 
> In article <3384AE16.740E@mail.idt.net>, Koji Hirano <koji49@mail.idt.net> writes:
> 
> :I would like to install either ULTRIX or VMS to the station, however,
> :all the manuals are lost and I have no idea how to install them. Could
> :someone tell me how to do this?
> 
>    See http://www.openvms.digital.com:81/ -- the V7.1 upgrade and
>    installation manual is there.  (This documentation will be for
>    a more recent release than you likely have, but there have not
>    been any major changes to the OpenVMS VAX installation process
>    in any recent releases.)
> 
>    You _will_ want a copy of the documentation in CD-ROM format,
>    and you will want to acquire (and read) a copy of the OpenVMS
>    Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ).  The OpenVMS FAQ is available
>    at ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/dec-faq/vms, among other
>    sites around the Internet.
> 
> :Another question is; I have one RZ24 hard disk drive, but the hard disk
> :drives in the station are RZ23. Can I just replace RZ23 with RZ24? There
> :are three RZ23 already installed and no more space is available in the
> :box.
> 
>    One can connect most RZ-series disks with storage capacities of up
>    to 1.073 GB to this system.  Do not connect a disk larger than 1.073
>    GB to any VAXstation 3100 series system as a system disk -- one can
>    conceivably have data disks that are larger, however.
> 

Larger disks work but are only recognized as DKX000 and not RZXX
I must tell you running VMS 5.5-2 and Motif 1.1 on a 3100 model 10 or 30
is a real tuning test.  Even with 16Mb memory a large swapfile is needed
and performance tuning is difficult. If you have a significant number of
Xwindow apps running it can be rather slow.

Maximize memory, limit your window apps where possible and dedicate the
RZ23 as your swap disk. You will become familiar with autogen by
default! Best of luck...
Tony



