I'm not a VAX expert, but from what I've read, the VAX 8000 series 
require three-phase power, and there is no workaround. The 6000 series
uses a three-phase power controller, which then basically provides
single-phase to various sections in the cabinet. I have conversion
instructions for the 6000 to allow operating it on 220V single-phase.

