In days of old, when 2060 was running a chess program that was not bad, I 
ran a pdp8 running a chess program from decus against the 2060.  Now, the 
8 was a good little machine.  It had an eae in it so it went along ok.  
When the 20 started loosing it did the following:
Informed me games were not supposed to be run during prime compute time.
as the 20s position got worse, it advised more frequently,  it said
the operator was being informed, then when the 8 had a good advantage,
it said:
System going down!
POWERFAIL
POWERFAIL
POWERFAIL
and line went dead.
the vt05 on the desk said it was still up and running.  My port to the
8 was dead.

So, sometimes dec machines cheat.

