I have a problem with sl_send_req.
I have a threaded application which uses IMS and it attachs to an MRQ.
One thread reads a request from the MRQ by issuing (roughly speaking):

while (!done)
{
	sl_wait_req

	if (status != PAMS_TIMEOUT)
 	{
		sl_get_msg_elt
		sl_get_req_elt * 10

		create thread to process request

		sl_finish_req
	}
}

It then changes the sl_wait_req mask just to read from the private queue,
until the
request is processed.


Once the thread has processed the request, it sends back its response
by issuing:

sl_create_req
sl_put_req_elt * 10
sl_send_req

After each call to an IMS routine I test the status and they all return
SL_C_NORMAL.

But, after about 30 transactions the sl_send_req returns SL_C_NOMESSAGE.

#define SL_C_NOMESSAGE     136020010L

From then on most (or all) sl_send_req's fail with the same error code.

Anyone know what the actual cause of the SL_C_NOMESSAGE?
Anyone had similar experiences?
Any solutions?

Cheers, Gary

System details.

OpenVMS Alpha V7.0
DEC C V5.3-006
DECthreads version V3.13-314
DECmessageQ for OpenVMS Alpha V3.2A-22(3222)




