Troy Richards (richards@edrd.dnd.ca) wrote:
: Hello Group,

:  Will a ZLXp-E1 or ZLXp-E2 work in a Compaq Pentium 5133 (which has PCI
: slots).

I imagine the problem would be that the Compaq's BIOS would look for
a VGA card and, not finding it, would refuse to work.  An idea to try
might be to install a cheap ISA or PCI VGA card as well, and see if your
operating system will let you use the TGA card after booting.

On another thread, the Linux-GGI project has an interesting solution to
multiple video card support that might be the only option at this point.
Unfortunately, the GGI project is still in an unrefined state and
probably doesn't support the TGA yet.

