In article <1997May21.171439@news.all-net.net>, byer@mail.all-net.net (Robert Byer) writes:
> -----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----
> 
> 
> Hi.
> 
> I'm trying to port over a Unix application to VMS using GNU C v2.7.1 and
> so far it's going great.
> 
> But, I don't have the "unlink" function which is kinda vital for this
> application.
> 
> My question is, what is the equiv of the Unix "unlink" in GNU C v2.7.1
> for VMS or for that matter VAXC.
> 
> I don't know all that much acout Unix programming or VAX programming so
> I would appreciate any and all help on this.

Try:


/*      Fudge to allow the UNIX unlink() to work        */
#include <descrip.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <lib$routines.h>
unlink(filename)
char *filename;
{
    static struct dsc$descriptor_s file_desc;
    file_desc.dsc$w_length = strlen(filename);
    file_desc.dsc$b_dtype  = DSC$K_DTYPE_T;
    file_desc.dsc$b_class  = DSC$K_CLASS_S;
    file_desc.dsc$a_pointer= filename;
    return (lib$delete_file(&file_desc));
}

(Extracted from XVMS utils Unix emlulation routines)

Patrick

