    	nenglish@axp1.umkc.edu (NICOLE ENGLISH) writes:

        I think this would better have been posted to comp.os.vms...

> We are checking into the possibility of using a 3rd party software to do
> backups on VMS 7.0;
 
        Why would you want to do that?   That is, what are you trying to
    achieve?   It's  very important that you specify your  requirements.
    VMS Backup, if somewhat arcane in its command syntax by current  DCL
    standards (since it dates from some of the very earliest versions of
    VMS),  _is_  _reliable_.   It  _will_ protect your data (by doing an
    end-to-end verification, as  well  as  keeping  redundant blocks for
    error recovery, etc.).  Is your data important to you?

> Is there such an animal...?

        Possibly, but  more  likely  in  the  realm  of archival storage
    (which is a different requirement than backups), and possibly access
    to robotic storage.  Again, what are your requirements?

> any recommendations...?

        Stay with VMS Backup.  If  you  need  to  access  a robot, or if
    you've  got some sort of archive needs, look into 3rd party products
    _and_ Digital's products as well.

        -Ken
