> 2 fixed frequency monitors - one under Linux, the other under Win95.
> 
> You just need to get the right refresh rates and mode lines.

Sorry, wrong.  DECstation colour monitors require sync-on-green.  Most
PC video adapters can't sync-on-green.  ou need either a card that can
generate sync-on-green, or external hardware to merge the sync and
green signals from the video card onto one wire (which often causes
signficant degradation of the video signal if not done properly.)

I use sync monitors on PC hardware myself, but not DECstation monitors.



