Perhaps you are twitting Andy over his team spirit; that is what I read
in his defense of "intel" being able to design ISA's well.  Asking
pardon for the perhaps pejorative reference, "jocks hire jocks, jerks
hire jerks, etc." explains (to my infantile satisfaction) why it is
appropriate to defend one's team as being composed of "uniformly good"
designers.  Exceptions do occur; you can get an occasional burst of
genius virtually anywhere, and an occasional lapse of same ditto.  But,
if you will, the image of a team doing a Borg thing or all assuming a
lotus position to commune design concepts ethereally is only a colorful
way to express a fairly real end result.

In fact, I suspect that the sheer luck of starting with the right poker
hand of talents to seed the various departments of a new company, and a
knack for maintaining that winning culture and team excellence, is
prevalent in the very few silicon valley megasuccesses, and has done a
lot to separate them from the cast of thousands of also-rans.

