In article <5lklt2$nh8$1@uhura1.phoenix.net>, mike_st@iah.com (Mike Stubblefield) writes:
:Help... I seem to have a problem-- you hardware guru's listen up...

   I've set follow-ups to "comp.os.vms".

:I have a microvax 3900 in a BA123 box. I have MSCP devices in the following 
:addresses:
:
:RQDX3 - 772150 (assume you understand the 17 on the front of the address or 
:17772150 but I am truncating those for ease of reading)
:
:RRD-50 controller - 760334
:CMD CQD203 SCSI Controller - 760344
:TK50 controller -  774500
:DILOG DQ142 (pertec controller emulates TS05) - 772520
:And KDA50 controller set to 760374
:
:The problem is that the KDA50 won't attach to a device driver but will show up 
:as a used address with no interrupt vector in the SHOW QBUS console command

   Make *absolutely* *certain* you specify *every* Q-bus hardware
   widget present in the system in the CONFIG command -- this command
   is available at the console, and under OpenVMS SYSGEN.  Once you
   have the settings, then check the switchpack settings on *each* of
   the installed Q-bus controllers -- do not trust the displays, as
   these are "desired" settings, not "actual" settings.

   CONFIG and other commands are available at the >>> console prompt
   on the KA655 processor module used in this system, and at the
   SYSGEN> prompt on this or another local OpenVMS VAX system.

   Based on the RRD50, CMD, KDA50, and RQDX3 likely all emulating a
   UDA controller, and the TK50 emulating a TU81, and the TSV05
   emulating a TS11, here are the configuration settings:

	SYSGEN>  CONF
	DEVICE> uda,4
	DEVICE> tu81,1
	DEVICE> ts11,1
	DEVICE>  ^Z
	Device: TS11    Name: MSA        CSR: 772520     Vector: 224    
	Device: UDA     Name: PUA        CSR: 772150     Vector: 154    
	Device: TU81    Name: PTA        CSR: 774500     Vector: 260    
	Device: UDA     Name: PUB        CSR: 760334*    Vector: 300*   
	Device: UDA     Name: PUC        CSR: 760340*    Vector: 304*   
