Hi, I'm answering the questions posted for DEC Ada on Digital UNIX.
I'm not speaking for any other Ada '83 compiler, since I haven't
investigated any others.

I'm not familiar with hiprof.

pixie, when I last looked, has a restriction against programs using
SIGALARM, in them.  DEC Ada uses this to implement delay statements,
so any programs with delay statements can't be profiled using pixie.
