If the monitor has 3 BNC connectors and your cable has 5, then you'll
need some way of combining the sync signals.  The monitor probably has
sync on green or something similar (sync on all colors, maybe?).  I
have seen info on building a cable to combine the sync signals but
don't remember where off hand.  I did a web search on fixed frequency
monitors and found it.  Plus, having a manual for the monitor is
invaluable.  I'm currently running 2 IBM-6091-19 monitors, one from
Win95 using an AOC turbo scectrum (Weitec P9100 chip) and the other
from Linux using a Diamond Stealth 2000 Video (trio64 chip).

Steve



