Alexander Hausner <alex@hugo.bmg.gv.at> writes:
> 1) How large can the Systemdisk be? I know there is a limit but is this
> limit <= 1GB or < 1GB

  It's the limit imposed by 6-byte SCSI commands. As long as all of the
blocks the bootstrap needs to load are reachable with 6-byte commands,
you're all set (the probability of success goes down as the disks get
larger - a 1.1GB disk should work fine, while a 3GB won't work at all
(since the index file is in the middle [1.5GB] which isn't reachable).

> 2) Is it possible to boot from an external SCSI-CDROM?

  Yes, *if* the CD supports 512 byte sectors or can be jumpered to do
so. "Normal" CD's use 2048 byte sectors.

> 3) Is there any Free UN*X System running on a 3100 (I am very
> disapointed because NetBSD only runs on VAXstation 2000).

  Don't know. If the folks that did the VS2000 port are around, I could
give 'em some tips on VS3100 differences.

