> Has anyone used the Atom tools - hiprof and pixie - with executables generated
> from Ada 83 code?
> 
> Has anyone used the -om switch - says use it with cc which I guess passes
> it to ld - for post-link optimisation on executables generated from Ada 83
> code?

ATOM and OM should work on any code that is linked using DIGITAL linker and 
adheres to the DIGITAL UNIX calling standard.    'Officially', only 
DIGITAL's compilers are supported, but we usually try pretty hard to accomodate
'unofficial' stuff.

FWIW, the cc(1) -om switch actually does two things: it passes -om to the
linker (which causes it to generate a special form of a ld -r file) and then
it invokes the 'om' optimizer on that file.    

