In article <337d7f99.898001@nntp.netcomuk.co.uk>,
rstevens@netcomuk.co.uk (Rob) wrote:
> Has anyone here using a shadowed system disk ever come across a
> situation when (say with a two node cluster) one of the nodes decides
> that the system disk needs a shadow merge after a reboot, whilst the
> other does not...
> 
> What happens then is that node A (which thinks the set is fine)
> cancels the merge every time node B starts it... You end up with a
> loop of merge starts/aborts. The small slots node B gets allow the
> merge to take place _really_ slowly, or, more usually, another reboot
> makes the problem go away (or both nodes agree on a merge)
> 
> They are running VMS 6.2 (Cant remember the ECO's for VMS/Shadowing
> off the top of my head)
> 
> Any ideas?

I don't recognize this as being a known problem.
If you haven't installed the "Redhawk" ECO perhaps you should consider
doing so.  (this is the V7.1 Mount/Shadow driver backported to V6.2.
Both Mount and Shadowing were extensively reworked, and lots of outstanding
problems resolved)  I forget the official name of this ECO.

If you *have* installed the "Redhawk" ECO, you should escalate this problem
through normal support channels.  If you can, when you see the problem I'd
suggest doing the following to be of most use to the support people:

Get two people to press halt/^P both nodes at the same time.  Force both
nodes to crash (on VAX  >>> D PC FFFFFFFF >>> D PSL 041F0000 >>> C
on Alpha just >>> CRASH)  Save the resulting dumps for the support people.

-Mike



