First: NetBSD/VAX runs also on almost all Q-Bus based machines e.g VAXserver-
3xxx.
Second: There's a port for the 3100 in developement. Dunno if you can down-
load it yet.

You could look for a license of Ultrix 4.5 as these are sometimes very 
cheap (e.g. at Universities; I got mine for free, both License and Install-
media for VAX and Mips).
Ultrix works like a charm on this Hardware. But caveat: your Machine should 
have a minimum of 16 Megs Ram installed when you plan to run X11 on it.

Hope this helps.

So long,
