In article <337C8019.6106@barilla.it>, Sergio Ferrari <s.ferrari@barilla.it> writes:

:we have just upgraded one of our development alpha open vms boxes to
:version 7.1 of axp
:and we have noticed that some products and executable will not run. 
:for example ACMS v4.1
:the errors experianced is 
: ERROR ACTIVATING IMAGE
: SYSVERDIF - System Version Mismatch Please Relink
:
:must we upgrade our version of acms ?

   If that is the product that is causing the error, then you need to
   upgrade, or to "register" the image -- the software rollout page has
   various supported product versions listed.  For details, see the
   OpenVMS home page at http://www.openvms.digital.com, and see the
   http://www.openvms.digital.com/openvms/os/swroll/index.html rollout
   page...

:we have managed to get some products to work by adding records to the
:vms$image_version.dat file in sys$system
:which acts as kind of registry file.

   This "registration" is not a good idea in general, as the mechanism you
   are overriding is present for a good reason -- when you override the
   image activator's lockout of privileged software by "registering" it,
   you can potentially see system crashes and/or kernel-mode system or
   user data corruptions.  Only "register" images if the vendor tells you
   it is "OK" to do so...

   These lockouts are "blade guards" on privileged-mode code -- meaning
   this code knows and potentially accesses the internals of OpenVMS,
   internals that may have changed during the OpenVMS upgrade.

:the impression that is given is that they are using this file llike the
:old Ms-DOS SETVER !!

    No, that is not the purpose of the file -- the file is used to tell
    the image activator that a particular kernel-mode image is "OK" to
    run, even if it looks like it might not be...
   
:If any one has any info on this it would be much appreciated as we are
:trying to iron-out any problems before
:upgrading to 7.1 on live systems. anyone needing more info drop me a
:line

   ACMS V4.1 is supported on versions through OpenVMS Alpha V6.2,
   while ACMS V4.2 is supported for OpenVMS Alpha V6.1 through V7.1.
   See the rollout for details.

