A DECstation 5000 monitor will not work: it's a fixed frequency monitor.
At best, you could cook a mode-line for the XFree86 X server that will
generate the right signals for the monitor (asumming no other hardware
incompatibilities exist between the monitor and the graphics card).

>The alphas I've seen have
>monitors that come with PC compatible cables and do work OK.

I doubt that any of the old alpha boxes that were using TurboChannel came
with a monitor suitable for a PC.  The newer AlphaStations all come with
PC-compatible monitors (I have one such monitor connected to my PC).

