We are running UCX v3.3 in OpenVMS v6.2 on an alpha2100 with one FDDI 
interface:

WF0: 192.9.201.253 (255.255.255.0)

A Cisco router with the address of 192.9.201.247 (255.255.255.0) is attached 
to the FDDI ring via a concentrator. On the WAN side of the Cisco router are 
two class A subnets: 10.61.1.0 (255.255.255.0) and 10.61.2.0 
(255.255.255.0). 
We want to set up two static routes on the Alpha2100 to the two class A 
subnets.

In UCX, I enter "set route 10.61.1.0 /network /gateway=192.9.201.247" and   
the system accepts it and defines the route in the routing table.
When I enter "set route 10.61.2.0 /network /gateway=192.9.201.247" to   
define the 2nd static route, the system returns the following error   
messages:
%UCX-E-ROUTEERROR, ERROR processing ROUTE request
 -UCX-E-DUPRECORD, DUPLICATE information
 -UCX-I-DESTGATE, Destination:10.61.2.0, Gateway:192.9.201.247
 -SYSTEM-F-FILALRACC, file already accessed on channel

Please tell me why UCX does not seem to be able to distinguish the two 
different class A subnets. Why UCX does not seem to allow different static 
routes to go through the same gateway?

Any suggestions, input are appreciated. If possible, please send your 
response to my office at sfung@cuedatawest.com.

Thanks,
Simon





