grossly over extended architectural design. The fact that Intel
was able to boost the clock speed above 200 MHz and get the
average CPI down to nearly 1 speaks volumes about the skills of
Intels engineers. I don't like the x86 architecture any more
than anyone else but you've got to respect the effort and
ingenuity it took to do what Intel has done with it.

- Jeff Dutky



