: Want to upgrade to VMS 7.1, but worried by notice stating that RF73 and
: RF31 drives must be at firmware > T392 or they will be unstable /
: unreliable.

[snip]

: Assuming that I need a firmware upgrade:
: - where do I get it?
: - how do I install it?

Starting with (I believe) VMS V6.2 there is a new subdirectory available
at sys$etc, which includes executables to (1) discover the current firmware
versions and (2) individual executables to do the update.  Just follow
the directions that you should find prominently in the release notes for
V6.2, V7.0, and V7.1, and you'll be done in no time.  This must be done
from a working VMS system on a disk that's dismounted from all cluster
members.  Obviously, this is kinda hard to do on your system disk, but
even there you may find newer versions of the VMS distribution CDROM can
boot up a minimal VMS system with no problem.

