The whole point of having patents is that the ORIGINAL idea has been
claimed legally by the patent owner. Even if one thinks of such ideas in
parallel, the first person who files a patent and was granted one basically
"owns" that idea.
The key in the legal sense (I think) is to prove that the defendent's idea
is the same as the patent owner as defined by the Patent Law (which I
cannot comment since I am not a Patent lawyer). So it is a matter if legal
interpretation (which can be leveraged by very smart lawyers argueing for
either side).

