After looking at your configuration below, I believe you have a RQDXn
distribution board from a BA123. On this board there is a jumper marked
"RX50" which can be moved to the alternate position to allow the RX50 to
respond to only one DeviceSelect signal(instead of the normal two),
allowing three hard drives(internally without using the RQDXE module for an
external drive[s]). 
RUMOUR:You may have to keep a spare RX50 floppy in the other half of the
drive to allow you to read any media in this configuration.(I haven't
tested this.Problem experienced by a collegue) 

Don't use media with reinforced hubs in the RX50 drive as it ruins the cone
that grips the floppy onto the hub. 
