Exactly -- you get a monopoly for a set period, in exchange for making
your invention available to all after that (rather than you keeping it
as a trade secret for as long as you can).

There's been some argument lately as to whether patent terms are way too
long -- in this industry (and some others), what was patented over
seventeen years ago may be no better than junk today.



