>Why is there such a difference in floating point performance for the
>chip itself and its system implementation? Why not integer?

Most likely L3 cache. I believe the motherboard used in the *au
line supports up to 2MB of L3 cache.  The 27 SPECfp figure is
likely for a more expensive motherboard with a load (8MB?)
of L3 cache.

