I can't fix the order of the listing, but this new version covers both
the keep level and before= requirements.  I dropped the ability to
write to a file in the com file, just assign sys$output to a file and
deassign it after the com file runs.  To get the listing of files
to be deleted if you say PURGE/KEEP=2/BEFORE=YESTERDAY, just say
  @NOPE *.* 2 "/BEFORE=YESTERDAY"
DCL is a surprisingly powerful language.

$! NOPE.COM - Display files that would be purged if you did
$!   a PURGE/LOG, but do not delete files
$! Dale Dellutri 1997-05-10
$! Version 1.2
$ say = "WRITE SYS$OUTPUT"
$ if p1 .eqs. ""
$ then
$  say "Usage:"
$  say " @NOPE <p1> <p2> <p3>"
$  say " P1 = filespec (must not contain version number)"
$  say " P2 = keep level (default is 1)
$  say " P3 = qualifiers for DIR command (do not use /LOG)"
$  exit %X10000002
$ endif
$ if p2 .eqs. ""
$ then
$  i = 1
$ else
$  i = 'p2'
$ endif
$ on warning then exit
$dir_loop:
$ dir'p3' 'p1';-'i'
$ i = i + 1
$ goto dir_loop

-- 
