The problem reported is in fact a problem with the old "ACC" compiler
on Digital UNIX. It is not a problem with DEC C, which is the default
compiler on V4.0 and can be accessed via "cc -migrate" on V3.2. The
problem in ACC (-oldc) has been officially reported as a "showstopper"
and is expected to be fixed in a future release.

The test case has been added to the DEC C regression test suite to
ensure that this never becomes a problem in DEC C.

