Subject: On Alphastation 255's/500's, random blank widgets.
Date: 1997/05/10
Message-ID: <5l0jgj$9ph@melb.werple.net.au>
X-Deja-AN: 240395291
Organization: Werple Internet, Melbourne
Keywords: athena xt expose
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec
Summary: Our application randomly pops up windows with some blank fields, xmon shows that expose messages are missing for these fields.


Hi,
I am having a problem with a large X app running on both Alphastation
255's and 500's with Digital Unix 3.2C and 3.2D.   This application
uses Xt and the Athena wigets. No motif.    The app displays 2D graphics
screens and is used contiuously.   The problem is that when there is a 
large amount of graphical data random windows pop up with random fields 
blank.  A mouse click in the field will fix this, also iconizing an bringing
back the window.   This fault never happened on the earlier Alpha 3000
machines running OSF/1.

I used the xmon program to look at the events for a window that pops up ok
and one that has some blank fields,  I found that for the good window all
expose events occur and then the text is updated in the fields.  For the
window with some blank fields we get text writes to the fields that will be
blank then expose events for all fields except those already written and the
text writes to all exposed fields.    Software people are saying to me that
this must be an O/S fault and it could not be in the app or in the athena
widget library.   I have included below the xmon listings for the same
window when it comes up ok, and then when it comes up incorrectly.  

Any ideas suggestions help would be appreciated.
Thanks for any info, I appreciated the time take to read this.

Peter Cupit.

