> I have recently come across an old tape back up drive (TK50) by Digital
> and was wondering if anyone had a program that I could use in order to
> make it comapatible to my home computer that runs Win95.

Well, I haven't ever heard of any sort of controller card for a TK50
that can be put on a PC.  I think that the interface on the drive is
totaly proprietary.  There are Q-bus (TQK50) and unibus (TUK50)
controllers specifically designed to control that drive.

However, there is hope.  There is a controller that makes the TK50 a
SCSI device.  If you can find that then you can just use the TK50 as any
ordinary SCSI device.

I'm not sure it's worth the trouble though... especially if you don't
already have SCSI.  Tape drives for PCs are pretty cheap nowdays.

