These are figures I know from the CRAY T3E 600 which uses 300Mhz Alpha 21164
CPU's.
              L1 cache -- cache line = 4 64bit words = 32bytes
              L2 cache -- cache line = 8 64bit words = 64bytes
In addition, the L2 cache is 3-way associative. The T3E does not have an L3
cache, so I have no information on the size of an L3 cache line. I would assume
that these numbers for the on-board L1 and L2 caches would be the same for all
of the members of the 21164 series ( with the possible exception of the new
21164PC which, I believe, does not have an on board L2 cache ).
                                           
