Hi Peter,

True, but the word from users on the AlphaNT mail list is that about the
only thing that *doesn't* work is the debugger (where all the
specialized code lies).  If you develop and debug under the Alpha
environment, then port to x86, you can (some of the time) get away
without having to run the x86 debugger.  I would presume that 95%+
coverage would be great for most developers -- send the x86 bins down
the hall to a coworker with a legacy x86 machine for final testing.

