Both.  I have managed mid sized networks using both Intel and Alpha
based machines, and I find a 300MHz 4100 with a single CPU and 128Mb RAM
will cope with the workload of 4 Pentium Pro 200's with 64Mb RAM each.

If you add extra processors or more memory to the Alpha performance goes
through the roof.   I look forward to 64bit NT5, as the current 32bit
operating system no more uses the Alpha's full capabilites that
Workgroups uses the Pro's.

I would strongly advise anyone interested in purchasing a server to
disregard SPECint and other benchmarks.  If anyone in Scotland would
like to see an Alpha in action, do not hesitate to contact myself.

