> 
> I have ported several programs from an SGI, running IRIX 5.3 and CC.
> These programs compile and run on our Alpha running 4.0b, with some of
> the output exactly the same as on the SGI.
> 
> HOWEVER, much of the file output seems to be either out of order and
> nonexistent.  This is all text using the << type output operators.
> I can follow the code in the debugger, and, for instance, if it is
> supposed to output the locations of 600 points, it goes through the loop
> 600 times, but only about 400 lines end up in the output file.  Then
> further output from later in the program shows up properly.
> 
> I am at wit's end.  I will see if I can find anything in language
> release notes about caveats, but would like to know if this is a known
> problem.
> 
> I have checked the public patches and the ECO CD-ROM, and believe I am
> up-to-date on everything.
> 
> Thanks for any advice.
> 
> Ed


Well, the Using DEC C++ notes say that:
	cout << "\n";
doesn't do a flush, since the C++ standard doesn't require it.
I should use:
	cout << ... << endl;
instead.
I tried it.  Apparently that is indeed the ticket.

I hope noone has to respond before they see the solution!

Ed


