This Alphaserver 1000 has been up 7 days now (that statement in itself
almost certain to cause a crash within the next 8 hours).  All that I
have done so far is to put a high-quality surge supressor on the AC power
and turn off Pathworks (PW functionality is actually used less than once
a month, I can restart/shutdown as needed).
 
I have also connected a LANalyzer and am monitoring the AXP1000 & only the
other stations that talk to it.  This being done with the hope that if the
EWDRIVER crashs are caused by the ethernet adapter acting like a lightning
rod to some incoming obnoxious packets then I can resend the packets to
myself and force a crash (a lot to hope for I know, but without any DEC
software contracts in place for any software on this box I have no other
choice).  I'm debating on turning Pathworks back on in another week to see
if I get an EWDRIVER crash shortly thereafter.
 
A few phone calls in the local area have yielded some actions that I will
take shortly.  One is to update my console firmware from its current version
V3.2 to V3.8.  The other is to bite the bullet and get a contract for VMS
software support.  Not being able to even use DSNlink hurts.  A colleague
ran a search on EWDRIVER & patch ALPLAN03_062 is just begging to be installed.
Between starting a software support contract on VMS & maybe doing an ala-carte
upgrade or two on Pathworks & UCX I think I can get ahead of the patch battle
here.
 
If this box goes back to crashing 2-3 time a week I'll update this post.
Otherwise we can say that no news is good news.
 
Thanks to all responders for posts and email,   Doug Braden



