We've recently submitted some SPEC results for Windows NT which show that
SPECbase numbers are roughly the same between UNIX and NT.  However, UNIX
has a lot of performance-tweaking tools not yet available on NT, so there
seemed little point in running the "all out" SPECint/SPECfp tests on NT,
where these tools (om, etc.) are used on UNIX.
