Sigurd Schelstraete wrote:
> 
> hello,
> I am trying to run a program (in fortran) on an alphastation 500 with
> digital UNIX 4.0A. This program previously ran on a SUN workstation
> without problems. On the alphastation, it runs for a while and then exits
> with the message:

I would suggest that you look very carefully for an uninitialized
variable (ATOM on the DEC or purify on the SUN will help).  The
Alpha is a bit pickier with floating exceptions that most other
machines (like the SUN).  Just loading an float value from memory
will cause an exception, where most other operating systems will
let you slide until you actually perform a mathematical operation
with the value.



