and are built to special Digital quality standards for shock,vibration, and 
thermal tolerance.(the RX50 also interfaces with the RUX50 disk controller 
for use in UNIBUS systems.)

The RX23 3.5-inch Diskette drive
The RX23 flexible diskette drive is designed for use in desktop systems.
It uses industry-standard, removable 3.5-inch microfloppy diskettes in both 
standard(70Kbytes formatted) or high-density(1.4 Mbytes formatted) form. 
The RX23 will read and write to high density media, and will provide read-
only compatibility with standard-density media, giving users access to a 
complete range of industry-standard published software on 3.5-inch 
microfloppies.

With a peak transfer rate of 250 Kbits per second in standard-density mode 
and 500 Kbits per second in high density mode, the RX23offers an average 
access time of 194 miliseconds. Data is recorded on 160tracks per diskette, 
with 9 sectors per track in standard-density mode and 18 sectors per track 
in high density mode. The power requirements of the RX23 are typically 0.22 
amps(at 5 volts DC) and 0.98 amps(at 5 volts DC) maximum when seeking.
"



