Another suggestion;

What is the nature of the application that it is still a 16-bit Windows application?

If you do not wish to compile natively to Alpha/NT for any reason...port the application
to Win32 and compile on the Intel platform.  You can then install DEC's FX!32 emulation
and translation/optimization technology on Windows NTv4.0 and run the emulated
Win32/x86 application which will yield far better results.

Of course, if the Win16 application does not follow the rules of acceptable programming
on NT, you should definitely fix the problems and just compile natively to Alpha/NT since
FX!32 will simply point out more problems in the Win32 version of "bad coding practices".


