In article <Pine.SOL.3.96.970505141355.26494C-100000@hammer.thor.cam.ac.uk> John Appleby <jma24@thor.cam.ac.uk> writes:
>I understand the SX motherboard is now almost available in the US; this
>only supports up to a 533MHz 21164NT, though, as I understand it.

There is no 21164NT, there is a 21164PC which will run NT, Digital Unix,
OpenVMS or Linux. The 21164SX motherboard does not pose a 533 Mhz limit
to the 21164PC clock, though the highest announced clock frequency is
533 Mhz.

>Is the 21264 going to be the full
>quad-issue or the 8-issue Alpha?

The 21264 is quad-fetch, 6-way issue and 8-way retire.

