Dan,
are you related to Scott Nudds?

The economics is not "How much ram can you afford to stuff into a machine?"

The economics is do companies want to pay programmers money to solve
their very large problems, or do companies want to pay programmers
a lot more money to solve the problem of how to handle the very large
problem before getting down to solving the very large problem in question?

Is this a good approach?  I doubt it, but as long as companies
want more stuff done on computers than the world has qualified
people to do the work, the intent will be to leave the thorniest
problems to the smallest group of people possible.

But remember, there are no computer needs, only computer wants.
