>I have several questions about Multia box.
>
>1. What is the possibility of using SCSI drive besides the 2.5" one? Has
>anyone been able to fit 3.5 inch 1" height hard drive inside Multi? What
>about power for the drive. 
>
The 3.5 inch drive comes with a mounting bracket that fills the space
otherwise reserved for a PCI device.  This box also comes with a
different backplane ... including only the internal scsi connector and
a small power jack for the hard drive.  A special cable connects 
between the backplane and HD power input.  

Part number for the backplane is 54-22563-01.  P/n for the bracket
might be 74-49232-01 but don't hold me to it.

>3. Can Multia be used in Europe? Does it have a switchable power supply.
>

The power supply says 100 to 120 vac and 220 to 240 vac, and I
saw no switches.  Perhaps it switches automatically?  The foreign
units ship with different power cords than the US units.  







