Newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec


We build petroleum exploration seismic analysis and mapping systems on
dual-headed AlphaStations running OpenVMS! 

Using the high compute, I/O and graphics speeds of Alpha, we process
huge amounts of data (seismic) in "real-time" and display contoured and
gridded 3D perspective maps in a live-linked co-operating process
manner.

There was a time when the upstream oil and gas industry was dominated
with Vaxes processing seismic data.  We're working to bring Digital back
into this industry because geoscientists need the fastest computational
and graphics hardware if they want to run new technology that features
real-time, live-linked, intelligently-integrated applications like ours.

Last month we demo'd our product line on a 500 Mhz AlphaStation...you
should have seen the look on their faces as we animated seismic traces
in real-time!

I'm not sure of the state of the rest of the computing world, but in oil
and gas, we hear of many, many support problems that appear to be UNIX
(or SUN) -related.  The oil and gas industry also appears to have a poor
understanding of Digital's offerings.  

At trade shows that Digital used to attend with dozens of technical
sales reps, it now is totally unrepresented except for software partners
like us.  It is odd, considering that the energy sector spends huge
amounts of $$$ in computer technology and yet Digital does not pursue
this market aggressively.  There are those in Digital that understand
that this market could be rewarding, but they're usually not in a
position to affect corporate direction.  (Our appreciative thanks to
those who try!)

Advertising would certainly help, but vertical market focus could also
help Digital regain market share.  Regarding OpenVMS as an equal product
along with NT and UNIX would also improve their competitiveness.  To be
frank, our end-users don't really care who makes the box or what
operating system it runs.  They want powerful, easy-to-use applications
that they can use effectively, and hardware technology that is stable
and RELIABLE.  

Digital has OpenVMS on Alpha now! ... Digital: Be proud of this most
excellent technology!

Mark Sun
Genetek Earth Research
marksun@genetek.com
