It's called em86.  It is based on the guts of FX!32 and was ported
by Jim Paradis (thanks Jim!) inside of DEC.  It's a binary only
release, but it's freely redistributable as far as I know.  It
currently only emulates, but I think it may end up getting extended
to do the caching that FX!32 does, too.  Of course, with 600Mhz
21164's coming out, who cares?  ;-)


