operating systems.

The customer then gets his free OS from one source or another and installs
it himself.  The customer is happy because he didn't have to pay for a
useless software product, the vendor cannot be held liable for the OS
crashes (unless they're caused by hardware failures).  It's perfectly
sensible, but don't expect any big workstation vendor to sell complete
systems without forcing you to pay for some OS, anytime soon.

Dan
